
=== 1. env --help (seven verbs, hidden rm) ===
Usage: pix env <command>

Named launch contexts: ls | add | use | show | edit | review | forget.

A named launch context: what runs, what mounts, which models, which MCP servers.
See docs/design/environments.md.

Seven verbs: ls, add, use, show, edit, review, forget. There is no 'pix env rm':
registering a name is not owning its files; forget only unregisters, and it
deletes nothing. All seven work now.

'edit NAME pix|sbxenv' opens pix.toml or .sbxenv.yaml in $VISUAL/$EDITOR (exact
positional enum, no flag), then reloads and validates: it never prompts to
accept a host-execution change inline: a changed footprint prints 'pix env
review NAME' as the next step instead.

An environment that runs code on your host or hands it a credential halts at
'pix env review NAME': y/N, default No. A non-TTY review fails closed unless
--yes.

Flags:
  -h, --help    Show context-sensitive help.

Config & context
  env ls [flags]
    List registered environments. Marks the default.

  env add <name> [<path>] [flags]
    Register a directory, or scaffold a new one, then review it.

  env use <name>
    Set the machine default. Refuses an unaccepted Tier1 environment, or one
    whose footprint changed since review.

  env show [<name>] [flags]
    What NAME is: files, models, mounts, MCP, review state, drift.

  env edit <name> [<target>]
    Open pix.toml or .sbxenv.yaml in $VISUAL/$EDITOR, then validate.

  env review <name> [flags]
    Read and accept what NAME runs on your host.

  env forget <name>
    Unregister NAME. Never deletes the environment directory.
exit=0

=== 2. env ls (empty) ===
no environments registered; pix runs with its own built-in defaults.
register one: pix env add <name> [path]
exit=0

=== 3. env add home (scaffold, tier0) ===
/tmp/wave-c-run/xdg-data/pix/envs/home
pix: environment "home" scaffolded at /tmp/wave-c-run/xdg-data/pix/envs/home.

pix env use home
exit=0

=== 4. env show home ===
environment "home"
  root:      /tmp/wave-c-run/xdg-data/pix/envs/home
  files:     .sbxenv.yaml
  declares:  0 models, 0 mounts, 0 MCP servers
  review:    not-required (nothing runs on your host)
  sandbox:   unknown (live-launch drift lands with a later wave)

full rendered environment: pix env show home --effective
exit=0

=== 5. env show home --json ===
{
  "schema_version": 1,
  "environment": "home",
  "root": "/tmp/wave-c-run/xdg-data/pix/envs/home",
  "sbxenv_present": true,
  "accepted": false,
  "review_state": "not_required"
}
exit=0

=== 6. env show home --path ===
/tmp/wave-c-run/xdg-data/pix/envs/home
exit=0

=== 7. env ls after add ===
NAME  DEFAULT  REVIEW  ROOT
home           n/a     /tmp/wave-c-run/xdg-data/pix/envs/home
exit=0

=== 8. env use home (tier0 not_required) ===
pix: environment "home" is now the default.
exit=0

=== 9. env ls shows default marker ===
NAME  DEFAULT  REVIEW  ROOT
home  *        n/a     /tmp/wave-c-run/xdg-data/pix/envs/home
exit=0
